    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n63469" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λῐπάρα</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾰ], ἡ</span>, <u>Lipara</u>, the
		largest of the Aeolian islands, <i><span class="en">
			Th.
			3.88
		</span></i>, etc.:—Adj.
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λῐπᾰραῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of Lipara</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ Λ. νῆσοι</span>
			<i>the group of these islands</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.25.4
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Λιπαραίων πόλις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mete.</u>
					367a6
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίθος Λιπαραῖος</span> a stone
				like
			<i>volcanic glass</i> or <i>obsidian</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Lap.</u>
				14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>L.</u>
				692
			</span></i>.</div>
